        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model with state transition function almost linear in xn for some range of θ, from which y1:T is",
      "bbox": [
        69.10992431640625,
        334.9174499511719,
        438.2219543457031,
        345.3274841308594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "considered to result, and strongly non-linear elsewhere. If the PG samples θ.i/ in those regions of",
      "bbox": [
        69.1102294921875,
        344.8800048828125,
        438.22198486328125,
        353.9450378417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "strong non-linearity, the particle tree is likely to coalesce on the trajectory preserved by the condi-",
      "bbox": [
        69.11026000976562,
        355.5957336425781,
        438.2299499511719,
        363.9075927734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tional SMC sampler, leaving it with a high importance weight, maintaining .θ.i+1/, x1:T .i+1//=",
      "bbox": [
        69.11026000976562,
        364.80511474609375,
        438.22222900390625,
        374.5847473144531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".θ.i/, x1:T .i// over several iterations. Using a PMH within PG algorithm would help to escape this",
      "bbox": [
