        438.2246398925781,
        384.54736328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "region, especially using partial rejection control and adaptive SMC kernels, outlined in another",
      "bbox": [
        69.11102294921875,
        385.4837951660156,
        438.2246398925781,
        393.795654296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "comment, to ﬁght the degeneracy of the ﬁlter and the high variance of ˆpθ.y1:T /.",
      "bbox": [
        69.11102294921875,
        395.44635009765625,
        368.1524963378906,
        405.2169189453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ralph S. Silva and Robert Kohn (University of New South Wales, Sydney), Paolo Giordani (Sveriges",
      "bbox": [
        42.708953857421875,
        419.20489501953125,
        414.2532653808594,
        427.5167541503906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Riksbank) and Michael K. Pitt (University of Warwick, Coventry)",
      "bbox": [
        42.708953857421875,
        429.1674499511719,
        287.8915710449219,
        437.47930908203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We congratulate the authors on their important paper which opens the way for a uniﬁed method for",
      "bbox": [
        42.70985412597656,
        439.1300354003906,
        438.22314453125,
        447.44189453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bayesian inference using the particle ﬁlter and should allow for inference for models which are difﬁcult to",
      "bbox": [
        42.70985412597656,
        449.09259033203125,
        438.2284240722656,
        457.4044494628906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "estimate by using other methods. To establish notation and to summarize the result that is relevant to our",
      "bbox": [
        42.70985412597656,
        459.0551452636719,
        438.2320861816406,
        467.36700439453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "discussion, let p.y|θ/ be the correct but intractable likelihood with ˆp.y|θ/=f.y|θ, u/ its approximation by",
      "bbox": [
        42.70985412597656,
        468.2645568847656,
        438.22412109375,
        477.32958984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the particle ﬁlter, where u is a set of latent variables. By Del Moral (2004),",
      "bbox": [
        42.709869384765625,
        478.9803161621094,
        321.83209228515625,
        487.29217529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0006",
      "bbox": [
        187.7153778076172,
        488.02471923828125,
        192.83518981933594,
        496.9911193847656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "f.y|θ, u/f.u/du=p.y|θ/:",
      "bbox": [
        196.93104553222656,
        500.2288818359375,
        293.2221374511719,
        509.2939147949219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The authors show that this implies that f.θ|y/=p.θ|y/ so a Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation based",
      "bbox": [
        42.71165466308594,
        522.2315673828125,
        438.2259521484375,
        531.2965698242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on the posterior f.θ, u|y/ gives iterates of θ from the correct marginal posterior p.θ|y/. Our own research",
      "bbox": [
        42.71258544921875,
        532.1941528320312,
        438.225830078125,
        541.2591552734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reported in Silva et al. (2009) applies the fundamental insight in the current paper to study the behaviour",
      "bbox": [
        42.713470458984375,
        542.909912109375,
        438.23486328125,
        551.2217407226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of adaptive sampling schemes when the particle ﬁlter is used to obtain f.y|θ, u/ for state space models.",
      "bbox": [
        42.713462829589844,
        552.1192626953125,
        438.2267761230469,
        561.1842651367188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The two adaptive samplers that we consider are a three-component version of the adaptive random-walk",
      "bbox": [
        42.714385986328125,
        562.8350219726562,
        438.2295227050781,
        571.1468505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "proposal of Roberts and Rosenthal (2009) and the adaptive independent Metropolis–Hastings proposal",
      "bbox": [
        42.714385986328125,
        572.797607421875,
        438.2312927246094,
        581.1094360351562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of Giordani and Kohn (2008). Combining the particle ﬁlter with adaptive sampling is attractive because",
      "bbox": [
        42.714385986328125,
        582.7601318359375,
        438.2330322265625,
        591.0719604492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "f.y|θ, u/ is a stochastic non-smooth function of θ. Our results suggest the following.",
      "bbox": [
        42.714385986328125,
        591.9695434570312,
        360.3653869628906,
        601.0345458984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(a) It is feasible to use adaptive sampling for the particle Markov chain Monte Carlo and in particular",
      "bbox": [
        52.378387451171875,
        609.5069580078125,
        438.2347717285156,
        617.8187866210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "particle marginal Metropolis–Hastings algorithm.",
      "bbox": [
        67.62126922607422,
        619.469482421875,
        257.1888732910156,
        627.7813110351562
      ],
      "direction": [
